Found in k198. waitForEndpoint in cmd/launcher/bridge.go logs "is reachable" on a bare TCP connect. The toolkit serves GET /mcp/status with toolCount, projectName and engineVersion (UnrealClaudeMCPServer.cpp at 9f6a0f7); that is the only thing that tells the toolkit from another listener on 3000, and it shows whether tools are registered. If the toolkit cannot start its server the editor only logs an error and runs on. The launcher never passes -MCPPort=, so a changed port must be mirrored by hand in UNREAL_MCP_URL.

Decision inside the card: use a status GET for the editor endpoint only and keep the bare connect for http/sse extra servers. Owner: unreagent-worker. Done when: the editor endpoint check reads /mcp/status and reports the tool count, with a test against a local HTTP stub; the bare connect remains the fallback when the status route answers 404.

Measured on Windows 2026-11-22 while running k202/k208 (Windows 11 26H2 build 26300.9711, UE 5.7.4 CL 51494982 Launcher, UE LLM Toolkit 1.1.0 binary, BuildId 47537391, in a disposable Blueprint project; editor started directly). Probe: TCP connect to 127.0.0.1:3000 every 0.25 s; after the first accept, GET /mcp/tools with a 2 s timeout until 200. Raw timelines: C:\Temp\unreagent-probe\runs\ on that machine.
- First start of a fresh project: TCP accepted at 48.5 s; GET timed out five times (50.8-59.9 s); 200 with 43 tools at 60.2 s, the same moment as the first game-thread tick (60.1 s).
- Warm starts (8 runs): TCP accepted at 10.0-12.4 s, 200 at 13.4-19.1 s, i.e. 2-7 s after the connect, always within ~0.3 s of the first game-thread tick. When it answers, all 43 tools are listed.
- Start without -unattended after a crash (modal "Restore Packages" dialog, see k202): TCP accepted at 10.4 s, every GET timed out for 150 s, the game thread was blocked. A bare connect reports "is reachable" here although no tool can run.
For the card: the status GET needs a read timeout and retries. During startup the route neither answers nor returns 404, so a timeout must not count as "not the toolkit" and must not end the watch. The listener is up seconds before HTTP is served (requests are handled on the game thread), so only a 200 says the editor can work.

Scout read of the UE 5.8.4 engine source on 2026-11-22 (source only, nothing run; paths relative to the engine root). Candidate readiness signal: PostEngineInit modules (the toolkit among them) load inside FEngineLoop::Init; the log line '(Engine Initialization) Total time' is printed after that (Launch.cpp ~175). It is an upper bound for 'module loaded', not proof the port is bound. Epic's Unreal MCP (port 8000) has no health route; a POST {jsonrpc ping} works without a session.

